@startuml UC-94 View Notifications - Sequence Diagram (icon)
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #000000
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 280
title 2.16.2.2 UC-94 View Notifications — Sequence Diagram

actor User
boundary ":NotificationsScreen" as UI
control ":NotificationController" as CTL
control ":NotificationService" as SVC
boundary ":NotificationRepository" as NOTIFS
boundary ":NotificationStreamPort" as STREAM
database DB

autonumber
User ->> UI : Click the notification bell and choose the unread filter
activate UI
UI ->> UI : load()
UI ->> CTL : GET /api/notifications?unread=&page=&size=
activate CTL
CTL ->> SVC : listMine(unreadOnly, page, size)
activate SVC
SVC ->> NOTIFS : findForRecipient(recipientId, unreadOnly, page, size)
activate NOTIFS
NOTIFS ->> DB : SELECT notification fields and read_at FROM notification_recipients JOIN notifications WHERE recipient_id = ? ORDER BY created_at DESC
activate DB
DB -->> NOTIFS : rows + total count
deactivate DB
NOTIFS -->> SVC : RecipientNotificationPage
deactivate NOTIFS
SVC ->> NOTIFS : countUnreadForRecipient(recipientId)
activate NOTIFS
NOTIFS ->> DB : SELECT COUNT(*) FROM notification_recipients WHERE recipient_id = ? AND read_at IS NULL
activate DB
DB -->> NOTIFS : count
deactivate DB
NOTIFS -->> SVC : long
deactivate NOTIFS
SVC ->> SVC : resolve the sender name of every notification and mark each item as read or unread for this recipient
SVC -->> CTL : NotificationPage
deactivate SVC
CTL -->> UI : HTTP 200 + NotificationPage
deactivate CTL

alt no notification is addressed to the user
  UI -->> User : Show the empty notification state (MSG01)
else the user has notifications
  UI -->> User : Show the notifications newest first, with the unread ones highlighted and the unread counter on the bell
end

UI ->> STREAM : Subscribe to /user/queue/notifications over the STOMP endpoint /ws with the access token of the signed-in user
activate STREAM
STREAM ->> UI : NotificationEvent of a newly created notification
deactivate STREAM
UI ->> UI : load()
UI -->> User : Show the newly received notification at the top of the list without a page reload
deactivate UI
@enduml
